DATA SOURCES

Each source is recorded as "copied" (its material may be in public/data.js) or
"checked against" (used to verify the data; none of its material is included).
The reasons below come from how the data was built and from comparing
public/data.js with the packages named on 2026-11-02.

JMdict/EDICT: copied
  Every common word and reading was checked against JMdict-derived word files.
  Where the English meanings came from is not recorded. All 581 distinct
  word and reading pairs in the data are in those files, and 396 of the English
  meanings equal a JMdict gloss word for word, so this is treated as copied. EDRDG's
  license names vocabulary lists as an example of a significant extract.
  Reached through: npm kanji-data 1.1.0 (MIT), from kanjiapi.dev (MIT).
  Terms: https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  Project: https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project

KANJIDIC: copied
  Readings and jouyou status were checked against KANJIDIC, and the second readings
  were hand-picked, leaving out rarer ones it lists. 149 of the 239 family-member
  meanings equal a KANJIDIC meaning word for word. Most are single common words, so
  this does not prove copying, but independent origin cannot be shown either, so this
  is treated as copied. The data holds on'yomi and English meanings only, and none of
  the contributed fields listed in section 8 of the license (such as SKIP codes).
  Reached through: npm kanji-data 1.1.0 (MIT), from kanjiapi.dev (MIT).
  Terms: https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  Project: https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project

Updating: EDRDG's license asks for a regular way to update from the latest files.
  .github/workflows/dictionary-check.yml compares the words and readings in the data
  with the latest JMdict and KANJIDIC each month and opens an issue for any difference,
  which is reviewed by hand. English meanings are hand-edited and are not compared.

KanjiVG: checked against
  Component trees were used only to confirm that a kanji contains its sound part,
  which led to corrections such as removing a kanji from a family. public/data.js holds no
  strokes, drawings or trees.
  Reached through: npm kanji 0.19.3 (MPL-2.0), whose trees are generated from KanjiVG.
  KanjiVG is copyright (c) 2009-2026 Ulrich Apel, released under CC BY-SA 3.0.
  https://kanjivg.tagaini.net/

The kanji-data and kanji packages were used as checking tools. They are not
dependencies of this project and no package code is included.


